*Description of problem:*

{noformat}See Service Mesh 3 Documentaion, section "2.3.2. Creating the Istio resource using the web console":
https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_openshift_service_mesh/3.0/html/installing/ossm-installing-service-mesh#ossm-creating-istio-resource_ossm-installing-openshift-service-mesh
After creating Istio CR via web console, status section shows "IstioCNI Not Found" instead of "Healthy" as suggested in documentation. As Istio CR is dependent on Istio CNI, this is expected.
Document snippet: "When State: Healthy displays in the Status column, Istio is successfully deployed.""{noformat}

*Version-Release number of selected component (if applicable):*

{noformat}{noformat}

*How reproducible:*

{noformat}Everytime{noformat}

*Steps to Reproduce:*

{noformat}1. Install Service Mesh 3 Operator via WebConsole.
2. Create Istio-CR
3. status section shows "IstioCNI Not Found" instead of "Healthy".{noformat}

*Actual results:*

{noformat}status section shows "IstioCNI Not Found" instead of "Healthy"{noformat}

*Expected results:*

{noformat}{noformat}

*Additional info:*

{noformat}{noformat}

*Background / Context:* Currently, the {{istio list mcp}} tool outputs data as a flat array of objects. Because it repeats the {{namespace}}, {{group}}, {{version}}, and {{kind}} keys for every single resource, the resulting JSON payload becomes unnecessarily large and verbose, especially in environments with many Istio resources.

To reduce bandwidth, improve parsing efficiency, and make the output more readable, we should restructure the JSON payload to group resources by {{Namespace}} -> {{Kind}} -> {{Validation Status}} -> {{[List of Names]}}.

*Current Behavior:* The tool currently returns a flat list where metadata is duplicated for every item:

{code:json}{
  "cluster": "api-crc-testing:6443",
  "items": [
    {
      "name": "ratings",
      "namespace": "bookinfo",
      "group": "networking.istio.io",
      "version": "v1",
      "kind": "DestinationRule",
      "validation": {
        "valid": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "reviews",
      "namespace": "bookinfo",
      "group": "networking.istio.io",
      "version": "v1",
      "kind": "DestinationRule",
      "validation": {
        "valid": true
      }
    }
  ]
}{code}

*Proposed Behavior:* Restructure the output to group by {{namespace}}, then by {{kind}}. For each kind, group the resource names into {{valid}} and {{invalid}} string arrays.

Example of proposed optimized output:



{code:json}{
  "cluster": "api-crc-testing:6443",
  "namespaces": {
    "bookinfo": {
      "networking.istio.io/v1/DestinationRule": {
        "valid": [
          "ratings",
          "reviews"
        ],
        "invalid": [
          "details"
        ]
      },
      "networking.istio.io/v1/VirtualService": {
        "valid": [
          "ratings",
          "reviews"
        ],
        "invalid": []
      }
    }
  }
}{code}

*Business Value / Benefits:*

* *Reduced Payload Size:* Significantly cuts down on duplicated strings (keys, namespaces, api versions, and kinds).
* *Performance:* Faster serialization/deserialization and reduced memory footprint.
* *Readability:* The hierarchical structure is much easier for humans to read and for UI components to process when building grouped views.

*Acceptance Criteria:*

# Update the {{istio list mcp}} tool's data processing logic to group outputs by Namespace -> Kind.
# Group resource names into {{valid}} and {{invalid}} arrays based on their current validation status.
# Ensure backwards compatibility if this endpoint is consumed by other internal Kiali services (update parsers accordingly).
# Update relevant unit/integration tests to expect the new JSON structure.

